<description>&lt;p&gt;CAR forces have completed Rwanda special forces and basic special operations training and have neutralised 34 Boko Haram and ISWAP fighters in the Lake Chad area, while the military chief held high-level talks with Rwanda Defence Force leadership. Sudanese Arab refugees fleeing to Chad near the CAR border are encountering hostility and distrust from local populations, and a man deported from Minnesota to CAR reports his life is at high risk. Misconduct has been reported at France's embassy in CAR and the government has declared a planned fuel protest illegal, while Sudan airstrikes are targeting border zones. The United Nations is planning a gradual drawdown of peacekeepers in the country. The conflict produced 246 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiugFBVV95cUxQY1pldmxNWi1fTzYzdXk5NlFWNDFmNGZTcDJkN0ROdmlOeTN4eEtlMlFhS0pWdzVKTzdyRGVSTkw5TFZmV2JHU20xajAxQkd4VHRXU0s4SmJ6ck9pcmRBZGFXcng5LW9aeHVqRzdiREZ6TGtoZ1lJeVhrYVNEZTNRS2dyZUZwcjBINzh5emVlb1BQcTUzVG5vNTViQXp6VjJTZ2dGTHY0NXg2TXR4LS1YUHNhbUhOanVtTXc?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMioAFBVV95cUxOUmxJSTBtNC0zNWtPUkRhQ1JxS2dCRndtN3o1cURid3ZkdTRjTmthSmRubHJONFNBYlFLT1MwVGVyUENyNnYyYTU3Rnp5YjRSa3Z0NWprOWl6ckx4T3hXS3dGeThhZjlzWHFZSDNrX2VabUlaZWhKQUJORlJBYlFqNTJNYWRCaWcxLWhDTkxIRVl2Q2JvYlFVajdlN050dlI0?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinAFBVV95cUxNU0Y3N3dwVkdGV1BpRmwxQ0FIYmYxVlRabkE2VU96bEVLMVhGVG01VTd6VDdpWFM0bktUSTZJczFsX2pHWWZ6SjN3RUVBbGRwaGJJUWtOUUFWcW1CUVV6bzItdjNHVm0zUmJ5VEI4RVhDLUV2RFV4Z3d5NGphSER3cXFBTHg3RDV3Smg4c0tUTVFTUHg0X2paSmRORWk?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;AZ Family&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news